Mission_11a has 0 MACultureSystem and 0 MACultureType objects, and no culture keys in MATerrain or MAEnvironment. It has 930 objects, 385 of them MACorporeal. 376 are foliage, all Env_NOR_Conifer02:
- 227 Env_NOR_Conifer02_Snow_Group (Env_NOR_Conifer_S_DS_Group.MGMODEL);
- 149 Env_NOR_Conifer02_Snow_Single (Env_NOR_Conifer02.MGMODEL). 373 of them sit under MAGroup 'Trees' and 3 directly under MATerrain. There are no world references or prefabs; the 33 MoeEntityReference objects point within the world. Mission_11b also has no culture: it has 648 conifers (369 Group, 279 Single). The ~466 traced foliage draws vs 376 objects is unexplained: the Group model probably draws several sub-meshes, or shadow/LOD passes add draws (inferred).

material env_rock_hesperus (material_complex) has spec_color 244,230,206 (F4E6CE). It is used on:
- KF: Env_Hesperus_Crystal_01_MP (bloom 0.3, C0.a 0x4C), _MP_DS (0.15), Env_Hesperus_Crystal_Debris_01 (0.3);
- M13b: Env_Hesperus_Crystal_01, _DS and Env_HES_RedTree01_Crystal_Group (0.2). So KF trace line 10124 is that crystal. The default material_complex spec_color is 206,227,242 (CEE3F2), and specular_bloom goes to the C0.a of the spec constant. the M13b trace's 7A7367 is exactly F4E6CE/2. Whether M13b halves the constant (a level or bloom-dependent scale) or uses a different instance value is not checked. Resolved (audit R2-17 #13, model XML): the spec constant rgb = spec_color x shin_strength, alpha = specular_bloom. env_rock_hesperus is 244,230,206 on every model. shin_strength is 1.0 on Env_Hesperus_Crystal_01(_MP) (bloom 0.30 in the KF MP version, 0.15 in 13b) and 0.5 on Env_HES_RedTree01_Crystal_Group (bloom 0.2). So the 13b trace C0 = 337A7367 (a 0x33 = 0.2, rgb = F4E6CE x 0.5) is the RedTree crystal group, not the spire.
